    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d175">

                <pb facs="0327" n="311" sameAs="frus:frus1950v02/pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">330.1/7–3050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bruce</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-07-30T21:00:00+01:00">July 30, 1950—9 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>542. Re Deptels 518 and 528, July 28.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d175-f1"/> I saw
                        Parodi<anchor n="2" xml:id="d175-f2"/> this subject yesterday and again
                    today making strong plea for favorable attitude. Schuman<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d175-f3"/> is absent until Wednesday night but Parodi had discussed
                    it with him. French attitude unfortunately characterized by great reserve as
                    communicated noon today to Chauvel of which you no doubt already informed.</p>
                <p>Department pass New York. Sent Department 542, repeated info USUN New York 3,
                    London 160.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bruce</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d175-f1" n="1" xml:id="d175-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 1, <ref target="#pg307">p. 307</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d175-f2" n="2" xml:id="d175-f2-content">
                <p>Alexandre Parodi, Secretary-General of the French Ministry of Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d175-f3" n="3" xml:id="d175-f3-content">
                <p>Robert Schuman, French Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
